On advice, sources and models
-----------------------------

This app is guidance and a draft, not legal advice, and every screen says so. It contains no
language model: the documents, dates, amounts and deadlines it reports are extracted from the text
the person pasted, and each one is shown with the sentence it came from so it can be checked. The
eligibility conditions are read out of that same text — the app has no scheme rules of its own and
will not judge eligibility when it can find no condition to judge.

The three draft templates (covering letter, RTI request, reply to a notice) are ordinary letter
shapes. Fees, formats, officer titles and statutory details differ between authorities; the drafts
say so and point the person at the official source rather than asserting them.
